# Captured data NEVER leaves this machine.
#
# data/ holds harvested session state: the SQLite store, raw status line payloads, and
# pre-compaction transcript SNAPSHOTS, which are verbatim copies of real conversations and
# carry session ids, account and organization UUIDs, working directory paths and file contents.
# It also holds a backup of the user's settings.json. None of it is publishable, and a private
# repository is not a good enough reason to put it in git history where it cannot be removed.
data/

# Scratch. Self-ignoring by convention in this project.
tmp/

# Per-project harness state (hook exec-state files), not source.
# The launch config IS source: it is how the app gets started.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Session records: the plan/result/review/verify trail this extension was built from.
#
# These are working documents, not repository content. They carry the machine they were written
# on - home directory, drive letters, unrelated project names, session uuids - and they describe
# process rather than the extension. A reader who clones this repo wants the extension.
#
# They stay ON DISK deliberately. They are the only account of WHY the code is shaped this way:
# why status line samples carry a probe flag, why windows are resolved per model segment, why a
# minified identifier may never anchor a claim. Read them before changing behaviour they explain.
.md/

# Research notes dropped in for review. Working documents about OTHER tools, not this extension's
# source, and they carry third-party product descriptions verbatim. They stay on disk, out of git.
Extension Features and Context Capture.md
Claude Code Context Capture Extension - Analytical UX Report.md
